# src/scripts/cloud-run-model-server.env.example
#
# NOTE (finding #4, 2026-07-01): the deploy script is now build+push ONLY —
# it no longer runs `gcloud run deploy`. Terraform is the SINGLE authority for
# the Cloud Run service, so the service-configuration overrides that used to
# live here (MIN, MS_MEMORY, MS_CPU, MS_PORT, MS_TIMEOUT, MS_INGRESS,
# MS_SECRET_NAME, the LUPIN_MODEL_SERVER_* model IDs) have MOVED to Terraform
# and are NO LONGER read by the script. Set them there instead:
#
#   Service knobs — GPU, cpu/memory, ingress, min/max instances, the secret
#   mount + KEYS_DIR, the scheduled warm/cool jobs, and the model-ID env:
#     src/terraform/modules/cloud-run-model-server/variables.tf
#     src/terraform/envs/test/{main,variables}.tf + terraform.tfvars
#
# The deploy script needs ONLY the shared GCP coordinates (project / region /
# registry / Artifact-Registry repo), which come from cloud-run.env via
# cloud-run-config.sh — NOT from this file. See cloud-run.env.example.
#
# This file is retained as a pointer only; nothing below is required and the
# script reads nothing service-specific from a cloud-run-model-server.env.
